From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: create the standard alpha and blend plane properties

MediaTek's v2 display driver attaches its own PLANE_PROP_PLANE_ALPHA and
PLANE_PROP_ALPHA_CON and blends from those, and never calls
drm_plane_create_alpha_property() or drm_plane_create_blend_mode_property().
The vendor hwcomposer, however, looks the two *standard* properties up by
string while probing DRM, and on not finding them gives up on DRM entirely:

  D hwcomposer: getHWCMediator default use full-hwc
  W hwcomposer: [DRMDEV] 0xeeeeeeee[34] property[alpha] does not do initialize
  W hwcomposer: [DRMDEV] 0xeeeeeeee[34] property[pixel blend mode] does not do initialize
  E hwcomposer: [DRMDEV] failed to check plane[34] property: error=-22
  W hwcomposer: [DRMDEV] failed to initialize plane[0]: 34
  ... once per plane ...
  W hwcomposer: [DRMDEV] failed to initialize all plane: -19
  E hwcomposer: [DRMDEV] failed to initialize drm resource

Having abandoned DRM it falls back to asking hwservicemanager for
android.hardware.graphics.composer@2.1::IComposer, which libhidl retries once a
second forever. Inside SurfaceFlinger that fallback resolves to the composer
service; inside a Linux compositor that loads the HAL in-process through
libhybris there is nothing to resolve it to, so the process never finishes
starting. On the Minimal Phone MP01 that is the whole reason surface-manager
never reaches its hwcomposer banner within its 90 s start timeout.

Creating the properties is sufficient and does not change what reaches the
panel: alpha and pixel_blend_mode are plain fields of drm_plane_state, set and
read generically by drm_atomic_uapi.c, and this driver's atomic_check and
atomic_update continue to blend from the vendor properties as before. Confirmed
on an MP01 (MT6789, E Ink): 16 planes, which previously advertised only
PLANE_PROP_PLANE_ALPHA and PLANE_PROP_ALPHA_CON to an atomic client, now also
carry "alpha" and "pixel blend mode".

Note when checking this by hand that both the vendor properties and the standard
ones are DRM_MODE_PROP_ATOMIC, so they are invisible unless the client sets
DRM_CLIENT_CAP_ATOMIC - use "modetest -M mediatek -a -p", not "modetest -p".

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor tree; MediaTek v2 display driver is not upstream]

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mediatek_v2/mtk_drm_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mediatek_v2/mtk_drm_plane.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include <drm/drm_atomic.h>
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_plane_helper.h>
+#include <drm/drm_blend.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fourcc.h>
 #include <linux/mailbox_controller.h>
 
@@ -603,5 +604,29 @@ int mtk_plane_init(struct drm_device *dev, struct mtk_drm_plane *plane,
 
 	mtk_plane_attach_property(plane);
 
+	/*
+	 * Also expose the two standard plane properties. This driver carries its
+	 * own PLANE_PROP_PLANE_ALPHA and PLANE_PROP_ALPHA_CON and blends from
+	 * those, so nothing here changes what reaches the panel - but the vendor
+	 * hwcomposer looks the standard names up by string during its DRM probe:
+	 *
+	 *   [DRMDEV] property[alpha] does not do initialize
+	 *   [DRMDEV] property[pixel blend mode] does not do initialize
+	 *   [DRMDEV] failed to check plane[34] property: error=-22
+	 *   [DRMDEV] failed to initialize all plane: -19
+	 *   [DRMDEV] failed to initialize drm resource
+	 *
+	 * and on not finding them abandons DRM entirely and falls back to asking
+	 * hwservicemanager for composer@2.1::IComposer, which libhidl then retries
+	 * forever. Creating the properties is enough to get past that: alpha and
+	 * pixel_blend_mode are plain fields of drm_plane_state, handled generically
+	 * by drm_atomic_uapi.c, so no atomic_check or commit change is needed.
+	 */
+	drm_plane_create_alpha_property(&plane->base);
+	drm_plane_create_blend_mode_property(&plane->base,
+					     BIT(DRM_MODE_BLEND_PREMULTI) |
+					     BIT(DRM_MODE_BLEND_COVERAGE) |
+					     BIT(DRM_MODE_BLEND_PIXEL_NONE));
+
 	return 0;
 }
